.TH alink 1

.SH NAME
.B alink \- link (relocatable) object files created by AS

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alink
[options] source [source ...] target
.br
.B alink \-help
.br
.B alink \-version

.SH INVOCATION
Use \-help to display current options and \-version for version information;
both exit successfully without source files. Input is read from named AS
code files, not from standard input. Quote paths containing spaces; supply individual source filenames
rather than tool-expanded wildcard patterns. Options apply to the entire invocation; word options are
case-insensitive and single-letter options distinguish case. Use + to negate
an option. Windows builds also recognize slash-prefixed options; Unix builds
accept absolute filenames beginning with /. Use the single-hyphen \-help
spelling, not \-\-help. Source names without an extension receive .p.
.PP

.SH DESCRIPTION

alink will one day be a the linker companion tool to asl.  It is work
in progress, and it won't be of much use for most users in its current
state.  Contact the author (see below) if you want to experiment with
it.

.SH COMMAND-LINE PARAMETERS

.TP
.B -v

be more verbose while linking.

.SH NATIONAL LANGUAGE SUPPORT

alink supports national languages in the same way as AS.  See the manual
page for asl(1) for more information about this.

.SH RETURN CODES

.B alink
may return with the following codes:
.TP
.B 0
no errors.
.TP
.B 1
incorrect command line parameters.
.TP
.B 2
I/O-error.
.TP
.B 3
An input file had an incorrect format.

.SH EXAMPLES

.SH TIPS
Run alink \-help for the option reference. A request without input
files is a startup error and does not prompt interactively.

.SH SEE ALSO

asl(1), pbind(1), plist(1) p2hex(1), p2bin(1)

.SH BUGS

In its current (incomplete) state, this program is a bug by itself ;-)

